# Semgrep's built-in defaults exclude test directories. That silently disabled
# the constitution's reflection rule — which applies to tests explicitly, since
# that is where reflection-based entity mutation actually happens here. A rule
# that cannot fire reads as coverage while providing none, so the defaults are
# replaced with this explicit list.
#
# Defining this file replaces semgrep's defaults entirely. Everything that must
# stay excluded is therefore named below.

vendor/
node_modules/
.git/
var/
backend-symfony/vendor/
backend-symfony/var/
frontend-react/node_modules/
frontend-react/dist/

# Generated or vendored assets
*.min.js
*.lock
composer.lock
package-lock.json

# Large fixture data, not code under review
scambuster-dataset-sample.json
backend-symfony/tests/fixtures/

# NOT excluded, deliberately: backend-symfony/tests/** and frontend-react/src/**
